<BaseLayout title="Šibenice privacy information — VCode" description="How the upcoming Šibenice game for iOS and Apple TV uses local settings, device motion and Game Center." lang="en" path="/en/sibenice/privacy/" alternatePath="/sibenice/privacy/">
  <article class="guide"><a class="back-link" href="/en/app-store/sibenice/">← Šibenice</a><header><p class="kicker">Privacy</p><h1>Šibenice</h1><p>Information for the upcoming iPhone, iPad and Apple TV game. Updated 28 September 2026.</p></header><div class="guide-body">
    <h2>Data on your device</h2><p>The game uses word lists bundled with the app. It stores your sound preference in device settings. Your chosen word and the current game are processed on your device; they are not sent to a VCode server. Uninstalling the app removes its local settings.</p>
    <h2>Game Center</h2><p>The game may sign in to Apple Game Center and submit a winning time to a leaderboard. Apple handles sign-in, player profiles and leaderboards under its privacy practices. You can play locally without signing in to Game Center; leaderboards will be unavailable. You manage Game Center data through your Apple account.</p>
    <h2>Device motion</h2><p>On iPhone and iPad, the game may use motion data locally to affect the game scene. It does not send this data to a VCode server. The Apple TV version does not use motion data.</p>
    <h2>Advertising and tracking</h2><p>The upcoming version does not activate an advertising SDK, show ads or track players across apps or websites.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>If you email <a href="mailto:podpora@zeleznalady.cz">podpora@zeleznalady.cz</a>, we use the information in your message to respond to your request. Do not include passwords or other players’ information. You can use the same address for privacy questions or to request deletion of a support message.</p>
  </div></article>
</BaseLayout>
